{
  "claim_boundary": "For a finite linear-reward policy family, a declared linear reward gauge supports quotient-level policy claims only if every policy occupancy difference annihilates that gauge. Under that condition, plug-in policy regret is bounded by quotient reward error times policy-occupancy diameter; a strict estimated-margin condition certifies policy identity; and the regret bound is exactly sharp on a registered two-policy witness. Composing with ASMP-9 v0.28 yields a measurement-to-decision factorization through the quotient spectral floor. Positive reward scale is irrelevant to fixed-MDP argmax but remains necessary for fixed-unit regret thresholds. These are classical feature-expectation, downstream-invariance, robust-optimization, and plug-in argmax ingredients; no novelty is claimed. The result does not show that a reward estimate is correct, that a registered policy is safe, that reward regret captures all safety loss, or that ASMP-9 is resolved.",
